{title: Our Dwelling Place}
{subtitle: Psalm 90}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm] |
| [Ab] [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Lord, you have [Bb/D]been our dwelling [Cm]place
Through all the [Ab]years gone [Bb]by
[Eb]Before the [Bb/D]mountains rose in [Cm]space
You [Bb]were, and [Ab]you [Bb]are [Eb]nigh
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You turn [Bb/D]us back to dust a[Cm]gain
Return, you [Ab]sons of [Bb]men
[Eb]A thou[Bb/D]sand years are in your [Cm]sight
Like [Bb]yesterday, like a [Ab]watch in [Bb]the [Eb]night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
We flour[Bb/D]ish like the morning [Cm]grass
By evening [Ab]it is [Bb]dry
[Eb]So teach [Bb/D]us how our days will [Cm]pass
That [Bb]wise our [Ab]hearts [Bb]may [Eb]lie
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Lord, you have [Bb/D]been our dwelling [Cm]place
Through all the [Ab]years gone [Bb]by
[Eb]Before the [Bb/D]mountains rose in [Cm]space
You [Bb]were, and [Ab]you [Bb]are [Eb]nigh
{end_of_verse}
